      {
        "Id": "0a49a23c29e3474db3960c94bd01717f",
        "Title": "What this graph does: It renames the elements you have selected in Revit. It adds text to the front and back of the name, and can swap out any text you want changed.\n\nBefore you run it: Select the elements you want to rename in Revit first. Then flip the refresh toggle in Step 2 off and on again ,if you skip this, the graph will use your old selection and nothing will change.",
        "DescriptionText": "",
        "IsExpanded": true,
        "WidthAdjustment": 1047.2538390691657,
        "HeightAdjustment": 4.879141235008888,
        "Nodes": [
          "0f94f5ed51db444c963b7b51e13e7928"
        ],
        "HasNestedGroups": false,
        "Left": -1987.5349990856932,
        "Top": -1866.4707050589473,
        "Width": 1127.2538390691657,
        "Height": 429.8791412350089,
        "FontSize": 36.0,
        "GroupStyleId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
        "InitialTop": -1490.4707050589473,
        "InitialHeight": 79.0,
        "TextblockHeight": 366.0,
        "Background": "#FFBB87C6"
      },
      {
        "Id": "d4c818dbb7b54a4b9fa3edbda35942da",
        "Title": "How to use it:\r\n\r\n1.Select your elements in Revit.\n2.FLip the refresh toggle off, then on.\n3.Type your text in the four boxes: Prefix (goes in front), Suffix (goes at the end), Find (the text to look for), Replace (what to change it to).\n4.Leave a box empty if you don't need it.\n5.Press Run.",
        "DescriptionText": "",
        "IsExpanded": true,
        "WidthAdjustment": 1060.4989324916392,
        "HeightAdjustment": 2.6358151536064724,
